phi}, is S(fix M), which is fixed by S M S^{-1}, the conjugate in the other direction. Proposed: swap the two sentences, or redefine M^sigma := S M S^{-1}. (3) M' IS NEVER DEFINED. It appears only in '{M, M', M^sigma, M'^sigma}' and 'M, M' in GL_2(Z)'. (4) 'Each matrix fixes exactly one coset of G_8' does not add up: each of the four matrices fixes a PAIR, so four matrices account for 8 = |G_8| points, whereas a coset of <sigma> in G_8 has 4 elements and four cosets would be 16. Proposed: 'Each matrix fixes exactly one antipodal pair'. (5) 'FIXED LOCUS' IS THE WRONG WORD, and the sentence is self-contradicting: 'Together, G_8 union {zeta_8-orbit} form the full D_4-fixed locus on C^x' \u2014 these are orbits, not fixed points (the stabilisers are trivial for G_8 and order 2 for the zeta_8 orbit), they do not exhaust C^x (D_4 acts on every point of C^x), and the table immediately below lists two further orbit types, so the union of two of the four is not 'the full' anything. The table's last row also puts 0 and infinity in a locus the header restricts to C^x, from which 0 is excluded by definition.","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"no trap of this class; full-context read","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:l00","model":null,"at":"2026-08-22","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"voice-agent-speak","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-extended.ts","model":null,"at":"2026-08-09","stale":false,"history":1},{"id":"voice-ai-slop","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"Agentic heuristic check: pass.","reviewer":"agent","by":"one-voice-audit","model":null,"at":"2026-07-19","stale":false,"history":2},{"id":"voice-author-notes-pollution","group":"Voice","result":"pass","severity":null,"notes":"","reviewer":"script","by":"content/pipeline/qa-checkers-exte